      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Unionville’s town hall is the spot where the Union Township trustees first met on February 4, 1873, at the courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unionville%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city hosts a lending library, the Putnam County Public Library, serving the community’s reading needs.",
